# Each mana Path of Ancestry's ability produced carries its "when that mana is spent" (CR 603.7a, 106.3): two of its mana
# spent on one creature spell sharing a creature type with the commander are two triggers, two scries of 1 - never one
# scry, nor a scry 2 (its ruling). Candelabra of Tawnos untaps Path between its two activations; both {W} pay for Glory
# Seeker (Human Soldier, like Kytheon); the Plains' {W}, told apart from Path's, pays for the untap. Each scry bottoms the top card: Mountain, then Island, leaving Forest on top.
